 a valuable technology in modern industrial operations. They support energy conservation, industrial innovation, and sustainable development by providing precise control over motor speed and torque. This leads to improved product quality, operational consistency, and process reliability.\n\n--- chunk 4 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What is the expected future direction of Adjustable Speed Drive technology?\nA: The future of Adjustable Speed Drives appears highly promising due to increasing industrial automation, energy efficiency demands, and technological innovation. Future Adjustable Speed Drives are expected to offer greater efficiency, higher reliability, and more advanced diagnostic capabilities, with developments in power electronics and digital control systems continuing to improve performance while reducing size and cost.\n\n--- chunk 5 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What factors contribute to the promising future of Adjustable Speed Drives?\nA: The future of Adjustable Speed Drives appears highly promising due to increasing industrial automation, energy efficiency demands, and technological innovation.\n\n--- chunk 6 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the benefits of using Adjustable Speed Drives in industrial applications?\nA: Adjustable Speed Drives provide improved efficiency, flexibility, and performance in industrial applications. They allow for precise motor control, improved speed variation, reduced wear and maintenance issues, and greater precision and reliability compared to mechanical systems.\n\n--- chunk 7 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the expected advancements in Adjustable Speed Drives?\nA: Future Adjustable Speed Drives are expected to offer greater efficiency, higher reliability, and more advanced diagnostic capabilities, driven by developments in power electronics and digital control systems.\n\n--- chunk 8 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What causes harmonic distortion in Adjustable Speed Drives?\nA: Adjustable Speed Drives can introduce harmonic distortion into electrical systems due to high-frequency switching operations. Harmonics may affect power quality and interfere with sensitive equipment.\n\n--- chunk 9 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the implications of harmonic distortion in Adjustable Speed Drive systems?\nA: Harmonic distortion can have significant implications, including overheating, reduced equipment lifespan, and potential equipment failure. It can also cause voltage fluctuations, impacting the operation of connected equipment.\n\n--- chunk 10 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the causes of harmonic distortion in Adjustable Speed Drives?\nA: Adjustable Speed Drives can introduce harmonic distortion into electrical systems due to high-frequency switching operations. Harmonics may affect power quality and interfere with sensitive equipment.\n\n--- chunk 11 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: Why is harmonic distortion a problem in Adjustable Speed Drive systems?\nA: Harmonic distortion can cause overheating, reduce the lifespan of equipment, and even lead to equipment failure. It can also cause voltage fluctuations, affecting the operation of other equipment connected to the same electrical system.\n\nYour job: for EACH chunk, decide whether it contains information that\ndirectly helps answer the ORIGINAL USER QUESTION.\n\nA chunk is RELEVANT only if a reader could extract at least one fact from\nit that contributes to answering the question. Tangential mentions of the\ntopic, generic background, or off-topic text are NOT relevant.\n\nThen give an OVERALL verdict:\n- "PASS"    : majority of chunks are relevant AND together they could plausibly support an answer.\n- "PARTIAL" : some chunks are relevant but coverage is thin or incomplete.\n- "FAIL"    : few or no chunks are relevant; the agent should retry with a different query.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no code fences) with this exact shape:\n\n{\n  "verdict": "PASS" | "PARTIAL" | "FAIL",\n  "per_chunk