2026-07-15 13:17:24 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | [-] | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e635a40a-4f9a-4335-9979-3730f4eea9d3', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are a strict relevance judge for a retrieval system.\n\nORIGINAL USER QUESTION:\nAccording to the knowledge base, which is more effective for ASD — ABA therapy or speech therapy?\n\nRETRIEVED CHUNKS (one per block, indexed):\n--- chunk 0 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the primary benefits of ABA therapy for individuals with ASD?\nA: ABA therapy has been shown to be effective in improving social skills and reducing problem behaviors in individuals with ASD. It involves breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors through positive reinforcement techniques. This approach can help individuals with ASD initiate and maintain conversations, understand social cues, and develop more effective social skills.\n\n--- chunk 1 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)?\nA: Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Occupational Therapy (OT), Speech Therapy, and Social Skills Training are recommended treatments for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder. These therapies can help improve communication, social interaction, and daily living skills. ABA focuses on breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors, while OT helps develop fine motor skills and sensory integration skills.\n\n--- chunk 2 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)?\nA: Recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder include Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Occupational Therapy (OT), Speech Therapy, and Social Skills Training. These therapies can help improve communication, social interaction, and daily living skills. ABA focuses on breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors, while OT helps develop fine motor skills and sensory integration skills.\n\n--- chunk 3 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What is the importance of a comprehensive treatment plan for individuals with ASD?\nA: A comprehensive treatment plan that takes into account an individual\'s unique needs and circumstances is often the most effective approach. This plan should be developed in collaboration with a qualified healthcare professional and may include a combination of therapies, such as ABA and speech therapy, tailored to the individual\'s specific needs and goals.\n\n--- chunk 4 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What therapies can help individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder improve their communication skills?\nA: Speech Therapy can help individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder improve their verbal and nonverbal communication skills. This therapy can also help individuals develop and improve their social skills, including initiating and maintaining conversations and understanding social cues.\n\n--- chunk 5 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What therapies can help individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder improve their communication and social skills?\nA: Speech Therapy and Social Skills Training are therapies that can help individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder improve their communication and social skills. Speech Therapy can help improve verbal and nonverbal communication, while Social Skills Training can help develop and improve social skills, including initiating and maintaining conversations.\n\n--- chunk 6 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the recommended treatments for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder?\nA: Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Occupational Therapy (OT), Speech Therapy, and Social Skills Training are recommended treatments for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder. These therapies can help improve communication, social interaction, and daily living skills. ABA focuses on breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors, while OT helps develop fine motor skills and sensory integration skills.\n\n--- chunk 7 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)?\nA: Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Occupational Therapy (OT), Speech Therapy, and Social Skills Training are recommended treatments for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder. These therapies can help improve communication, social interaction, and daily living skills. ABA focuses on breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors, while OT helps develop fine motor skills and sensory integration skills.\n\n--- chunk 8 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the primary benefits of ABA therapy for individuals with ASD?\nA: ABA therapy has been shown to be effective in improving social skills and reducing problem behaviors in individuals with ASD. It involves breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors through positive reinforcement techniques. This approach can help individuals with ASD initiate and maintain conversations, understand social cues, and develop more effective social skills.\n\n--- chunk 9 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are some key strategies for supporting children with ASD in their social development?\nA: Identify possible triggers such as sensory overload, pain, anxiety, or changes in routine, and provide a supportive and understanding environment. Remain calm, avoid confrontation, and use de-escalation techniques to help children with ASD develop the skills and strategies they need to thrive.\n\n--- chunk 10 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)?\nA: Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Occupational Therapy (OT), Speech Therapy, and Social Skills Training are recommended treatments for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder. These therapies can help improve communication, social interaction, and daily living skills. ABA focuses on breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors, while OT helps develop fine motor skills and sensory integration skills.\n\n--- chunk 11 (source: learned_qa) ---\nQ: What are the recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)?\nA: Recommended treatment options for individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder include Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Occupational Therapy (OT), Speech Therapy, and Social Skills Training. These therapies can help improve communication, social interaction, and daily living skills. ABA focuses on breaking down complex behaviors into smaller parts and reinforcing desired behaviors, while OT helps develop fine motor skills and sensory integration skills.\n\nYour job: for EACH chunk, decide whether it contains information that\ndirectly helps answer the ORIGINAL USER QUESTION.\n\nA chunk is RELEVANT only if a reader could extract at least one fact from\nit that contributes to answering the question. Tangential mentions of the\ntopic, generic background, or off-topic text are NOT relevant.\n\nThen give an OVERALL verdict:\n- "PASS"    : majority of chunks are relevant AND together they could plausibly support an answer.\n- "PARTIAL" : some chunks are relevant but coverage is thin or incomplete.\n- "FAIL"    : few or no chunks are relevant; the agent should retry with a different query.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no code fences) with this exact shape:\n\n{\n  "verdict": "PASS" | "PARTIAL" | "FAIL",\n  "per_chunk": [\n    {"index": 0, "relevant": true,  "reason": "<one short sentence>"},\n    {"index": 1, "relevant": false, "reason": "<one short sentence>"}\n  ],\n  "overall_reason": "<one or two sentences>"\n}\n', 'role': 'system'}], 'model': 'llama-3.1-8b-instruct', 'max_completion_tokens': 1024, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
