2026-07-15 13:17:38 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | [-] | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-271b1b8b-3f22-4b5b-9dbf-ccabe7cc5345', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are a strict relevance judge for a retrieval system.\n\nORIGINAL USER QUESTION:\nAccording to the knowledge base, which is more effective for ASD — ABA therapy or speech therapy?\n\nRETRIEVED CHUNKS (one per block, indexed):\n--- chunk 0 (source: ..\\data\\pdfs\\Autism spectrum disorder definition, epidemiology, causes, and clinical evaluation.pdf) ---\nInsurance mandates requiring commercial plans to cover services for ASD along with improved awareness have likely contributed to the increase in ASD prevalence estimates as well as the increased diagnosis of milder cases of ASD in\n\n--- chunk 1 (source: ..\\data\\word\\ASD_Patient_Management_Handbook.docx) ---\nAlways treat ASD patients with dignity and respect. Avoid stereotypes and recognize that each individual has unique strengths and challenges. Use person-centered care and encourage autonomy whenever possible.\n\n--- chunk 2 (source: ..\\data\\pdfs\\Autism spectrum disorder definition, epidemiology, causes, and clinical evaluation.pdf) ---\nverbal communication in children with autism and language impairment: a randomized double-blind placebo- controlled trial. Mol Psychiatry 2018;23:247-56. 59. Croen LA, Najjar DV, Fireman B, et al. Maternal and\n\n--- chunk 3 (source: ..\\data\\pdfs\\Autism spectrum disorder definition, epidemiology, causes, and clinical evaluation.pdf) ---\nparameter for the assessment and treatment of children and adolescents with autism spectrum disorder. J Am Acad Child Adolesc Psychiatry 2014;53:237-57.\n\n--- chunk 4 (source: ..\\data\\html\\asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html) ---\nReducing disparities among ASD patients requires action at multiple levels. Screening tools and clinical training should reflect a broader range of autistic presentations, especially in girls and culturally diverse populations. Providers should be trained to recognize masking, subtle social communication differences, and the ways autism may be expressed differently across communities. Diagnostic pathways should include interpreters, culturally responsive family communication, and patient navigation support for families facing practical barriers.\n\n--- chunk 5 (source: ..\\data\\word\\ASD_Patient_Management_Handbook.docx) ---\nThis handbook provides healthcare professionals, caregivers, educators, and support staff with practical guidance for understanding and managing patients with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD). The goal is to promote patient-centered care, improve communication, reduce stress, and support the emotional, behavioral, and developmental needs of individuals with ASD.\n\n--- chunk 6 (source: ..\\data\\pdfs\\Autism spectrum disorder definition, epidemiology, causes, and clinical evaluation.pdf) ---\nmay include limited pretend play, odd or intensely focused interests, and rigidity. School age children may demonstrate concrete or literal thinking, have trouble understanding emotions, and may even show an interest in peers but lack conversational skills or appropriate social approach. If there is suspicion of ASD in these groups, screening tools available include the Social Communication Questionnaire (SCQ), Social Responsiveness Scale (SRS), and Autism Spectrum Screening Questionnaire (ASSQ) (74-76).\n\n--- chunk 7 (source: ..\\data\\word\\ASD_Patient_Management_Handbook.docx) ---\nAlways treat ASD patients with dignity and respect. Avoid stereotypes and recognize that each individual has unique strengths and challenges. Use person-centered care and encourage autonomy whenever possible.\n\n--- chunk 8 (source: ..\\data\\html\\asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html) ---\nAutism spectrum disorder (ASD) is a neurodevelopmental condition associated with differences in social communication, restricted interests, repetitive behaviors, and sensory processing. Although ASD has received increasing clinical and public attention, the experience of being identified, diagnosed, and treated is not the same for all patients. Gender and racial factors shape who is recognized early, who is overlooked, who receives appropriate services, and who must overcome greater barriers before support becomes available. These disparities matter because delayed identification can postpone therapy, school accommodations, family guidance, and access to specialized care.\n\n--- chunk 9 (source: ..\\data\\pdfs\\Autism spectrum disorder definition, epidemiology, causes, and clinical evaluation.pdf) ---\nAutism spectrum disorder (ASD) is a neurodevelopmental disorder characterized by deficits in social communication and the presence of restricted interests and repetitive behaviors (1). In 2013, the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders—5th edition (DSM-5) was published, updating the diagnostic criteria for ASD from the previous 4th edition (DSM-IV) (Table 1) (1,2).\n\nYour job: for EACH chunk, decide whether it contains information that\ndirectly helps answer the ORIGINAL USER QUESTION.\n\nA chunk is RELEVANT only if a reader could extract at least one fact from\nit that contributes to answering the question. Tangential mentions of the\ntopic, generic background, or off-topic text are NOT relevant.\n\nThen give an OVERALL verdict:\n- "PASS"    : majority of chunks are relevant AND together they could plausibly support an answer.\n- "PARTIAL" : some chunks are relevant but coverage is thin or incomplete.\n- "FAIL"    : few or no chunks are relevant; the agent should retry with a different query.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no code fences) with this exact shape:\n\n{\n  "verdict": "PASS" | "PARTIAL" | "FAIL",\n  "per_chunk": [\n    {"index": 0, "relevant": true,  "reason": "<one short sentence>"},\n    {"index": 1, "relevant": false, "reason": "<one short sentence>"}\n  ],\n  "overall_reason": "<one or two sentences>"\n}\n', 'role': 'system'}], 'model': 'llama-3.1-8b-instruct', 'max_completion_tokens': 1024, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
