[5] ASD exists on a spectrum, meaning symptoms and support needs vary significantly between individuals.

[6] The goal is to promote patient-centered care, improve communication, reduce stress, and support the emotional, behavioral, and developmental needs of individuals with ASD

[7] Understanding communication differences, sensory sensitivities, and behavioral triggers can significantly improve healthcare experiences and outcomes for individuals on the autism spectrum [Source:../data/word/ASD_Patient_Management_Handbook.docx].

