2026-07-15 13:44:04 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | [-] | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-267813b0-1bdc-4598-a0ee-4538cc31bad5', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are a strict relevance judge for a retrieval system.\n\nORIGINAL USER QUESTION:\nWhat percentage of energy can a facility realistically expect to save by installing Adjustable Speed Drives on all its fans and pumps?\n\nRETRIEVED CHUNKS (one per block, indexed):\n--- chunk 0 (source: ..\\data\\Adjustable Speed Drive.txt) ---\nIn HVAC systems, Adjustable Speed Drives control fan and pump speeds based on temperature and airflow demands. This significantly reduces energy consumption because fans and pumps rarely need to operate at full capacity continuously.\n\n--- chunk 1 (source: ..\\data\\Adjustable Speed Drive.txt) ---\nOne of the most significant advantages of Adjustable Speed Drives is energy savings. By matching motor speed to actual load requirements, Adjustable Speed Drives eliminate unnecessary power consumption. In applications such as fans and pumps, even small speed reductions can result in substantial energy savings.\n\n--- chunk 2 (source: ..\\data\\Adjustable Speed Drive.txt) ---\nThe increasing emphasis on sustainability and energy conservation has further increased the importance of Adjustable Speed Drives in industrial and commercial sectors. According to energy studies, electric motors consume a significant portion of global electricity, especially in manufacturing facilities. By integrating Adjustable Speed Drives into motor-driven systems, organizations can reduce energy consumption substantially while improving process control and equipment lifespan. This essay explores the concept of Adjustable Speed Drives, including their principles, components, types, working mechanisms, applications, advantages, limitations, and future developments.\n\n--- chunk 3 (source: ..\\data\\Adjustable Speed Drive.txt) ---\nMany countries have introduced energy efficiency standards and regulations that encourage or require the use of variable speed motor control systems. As electricity prices continue to rise, the demand for Adjustable Speed Drives is expected to grow further.\n\n--- chunk 4 (source: ..\\data\\Adjustable Speed Drive.txt) ---\nIn HVAC systems, Adjustable Speed Drives control fan and pump speeds based on temperature and airflow demands. This significantly reduces energy consumption because fans and pumps rarely need to operate at full capacity continuously.\n\n--- chunk 5 (source: ..\\data\\Adjustable Speed Drive.txt) ---\nIn HVAC systems, Adjustable Speed Drives control fan and pump speeds based on temperature and airflow demands. This significantly reduces energy consumption because fans and pumps rarely need to operate at full capacity continuously.\n\nYour job: for EACH chunk, decide whether it contains information that\ndirectly helps answer the ORIGINAL USER QUESTION.\n\nA chunk is RELEVANT only if a reader could extract at least one fact from\nit that contributes to answering the question. Tangential mentions of the\ntopic, generic background, or off-topic text are NOT relevant.\n\nThen give an OVERALL verdict:\n- "PASS"    : majority of chunks are relevant AND together they could plausibly support an answer.\n- "PARTIAL" : some chunks are relevant but coverage is thin or incomplete.\n- "FAIL"    : few or no chunks are relevant; the agent should retry with a different query.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no code fences) with this exact shape:\n\n{\n  "verdict": "PASS" | "PARTIAL" | "FAIL",\n  "per_chunk": [\n    {"index": 0, "relevant": true,  "reason": "<one short sentence>"},\n    {"index": 1, "relevant": false, "reason": "<one short sentence>"}\n  ],\n  "overall_reason": "<one or two sentences>"\n}\n', 'role': 'system'}],