2026-07-15 14:24:40 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | [-] | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6b201356-b4a9-4966-9424-389debe83ccf', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You merge near-duplicate retrieved chunks into one consolidated chunk.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this shape (no code, no markdown fences, no explanation):\n\n{{"content": "...", "sources": [...], "merged_from": <int>}}\n\nEXAMPLE INPUT:\n[Source: a.pdf]\nASD affects 1 in 36 children. Early diagnosis improves outcomes.\n\n[Source: b.pdf]\nApproximately 1 in 36 kids have autism spectrum disorder. Children diagnosed early respond better to therapy.\n\nEXAMPLE OUTPUT:\n{{"content": "ASD affects approximately 1 in 36 children [Source: a.pdf] [Source: b.pdf]. Early diagnosis improves outcomes and response to therapy [Source: a.pdf] [Source: b.pdf].", "sources": ["a.pdf", "b.pdf"], "merged_from": 2}}\n\nRULES:\n- Preserve every fact across all input chunks. Never invent new facts.\n- Write each distinct fact only once, even if multiple chunks state it.\n- Cite every source inline as [Source: filename] after the sentence it supports.\n- If multiple sources support the same fact, list them all: [Source: a.pdf] [Source: b.pdf].\n- Do NOT write Python code. Do NOT explain your process. Output ONLY the JSON object.\n\nINPUT CHUNKS:\n\n\nINPUT CHUNKS:\n[Source: "../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html, ../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html"]\n"Racial and ethnic disparities in ASD are also complex. Older research often showed that Black and Hispanic children were less likely than White children to have a documented autism diagnosis in service records and were more likely to face delays, misclassification, or incomplete evaluation pathways [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html] [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html]. Barriers such as language differences, stigma, limited specialist access, provider bias, transportation problems, and weak continuity of care contributed to these gaps [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html] [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html]."\n\n[Source: "../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html, ../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html"]\n"More recent CDC surveillance data show a different pattern in prevalence estimates, with ASD prevalence in recent samples being lower among White children than among several other racial and ethnic groups, including Black, Hispanic, Asian/Pacific Islander, and American Indian/Alaska Native children [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html] [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html]. However, higher observed prevalence does not mean disparities have disappeared [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html] [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html]. Instead, it may reflect improvements in recognition in some communities while major inequities remain in the timing of diagnosis, quality of assessment, comorbid condition management, and service access [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html] [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html]. In other words, being counted is not the same as being equitably served [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html] [Source:../data/html/asd_disparities_gender_race_essay.html]."', 'role': 'system'}], 'model': 'llama-3.1-8b-instruct', 'max_completion_tokens': 2048, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.1}}
